            <ArticleTitle>Design and Application of a DNA-Encoded Macrocyclic Peptide Library.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acschembio.7b00852</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A DNA-encoded macrocyclic peptide library was designed and synthesized with 2.4 × 1012 members composed of 4-20 natural and non-natural amino acids. Affinity-based selection was performed against two therapeutic targets, VHL and RSV N protein. On the basis of selection data, some peptides were selected for resynthesis without a DNA tag, and their activity was confirmed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
